From 1d5adf1a321c507421c9b2dec4e97d918456d188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:08:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the findings of the review of the kernels and of the
 fixed point solver

- failures of the computation of the corrections (NonLinearSolverBase::
  callAndHandleFailures, used by the Newton and fixed point solvers): in
  parallel, only the failures reported on all the processes
  (CollectiveFailure) are handled, any other exception reaching
  std::terminate after its message is printed; the collective agreement,
  which could pair with another collective operation, is removed; the
  refusal of the tangent operator applied without assembly, the same on
  all the processes, throws a CollectiveFailure;
- FixedPointSolver: options read and checked before being applied, the
  elastic operator being computed again if its computation changes;
  ElasticOperatorLinearSolver refused with ModifiedNewton; Name/Options
  format accepted for the options built by factories; the actions
  associated with a new estimate are called once on the first estimate;
  information on the linear solver at each iteration, as Newton; the
  iterations stop on a residual which is not finite;
- Anderson: strictly positive regularization;
- documentation (one cycle of BoomerAMG in parallel only, convention of
  the correction given to the accelerations) and compiler warnings;
- FixedPointSolverTest: maximum numbers of iterations of the accelerations
  (a wrong acceleration which still converges is detected); variants with
  the integration by batches and the computations by kernels, on the host
  and on the debug device.
